
The CentaurHauls VIA Eden Esther cpu reports 80bit x86
extended precision for anything past 64bit and strangely
it uses 12 bytes of memory.  Perhaps because it is a 32-bit
machine ???

C_esther$ 
C_esther$ ./fmad
NOTE : this machine is a little endian architecture.
     : Be sure to adjust your brain accordingly.


--------------- Maybe no FMA Calls ---------------

        fp32  = +5.595782771706581116e-02
 dotme_fp32  is 0x09 0x34 0x65 0x3d 

        fp64  = +5.595788259857980423e-02
 dotme_fp64  is 0xbf 0xb9 0x6d 0xf7 0x82 0xa6 0xac 0x3f 

        fp128 = +5.595788259858000004e-02
 dotme_fp128 is 0xc0 0xd9 0xce 0x6d 0xbb 0x17 0x34 0xe5 0xfa 0x3f 0x00 0x00 



-------------------- FMA Calls -------------------

  fmaf fp32   = +5.595775693655014038e-02
 dotme_fp32  is 0xf6 0x33 0x65 0x3d 

  fma  fp64   = +5.595788259857976260e-02
 dotme_fp64  is 0xb9 0xb9 0x6d 0xf7 0x82 0xa6 0xac 0x3f 

  fmal fp128  = +5.595788259858000003e-02
 dotme_fp128 is 0xbc 0xd9 0xce 0x6d 0xbb 0x17 0x34 0xe5 0xfa 0x3f 0x00 0x00 


--------------------------------------------------


Correct result is +5.595788259858e-02
or this    0x3faca682f76db9b9 from ARMv8
or maybe   0x3faca682f76db9b9 on Fujitsu SPARC VII+
Same thing on Intel Core i5-7300U K8-class CPU
also fp128 0x3ffaca682f76db9db367bf4a016eb28a

NOTE : IBM Power systems may report strange fp128 hex values
C_esther$ 

